return {
    ["        罗塞尔·古斯塔夫已经死去一百五十多年了，但他的名字从未被遗忘。\n        在因蒂斯的首都特里尔，他的雕像依然矗立在广场中央。每年他的诞辰，人们都会举行盛大的活动来纪念他。鲁恩王国的工厂里，工人们使用着他发明的机器，孩子们在学校里学习着他推行的知识。迷雾海的商船沿着他开辟的航道航行，南大陆的殖民地里，冒险者们讲述着他的传说。\n        他是一个穿越者，一个异乡人，一个永远回不去故乡的游子。但他也是蒸汽之子，因蒂斯共和国的执政官，凯撒大帝，罗塞尔大帝，一个强大的非凡者，一个父亲——一个改变了整个世界的人。\n        他犯过错，走过弯路，被污染，被背叛，最终陨落于白枫宫。但他也创造过，保护过，爱过，留下过一个时代的辉煌与文明。\n        也许正如他在日记中写的那样：如果能够重来，他或许会选择做一个普通人，回到那个有炸鸡和可乐的世界，陪在父母身边，过着平凡而温暖的一生。但历史没有如果。罗塞尔·古斯塔夫无可选择地成为时代的主角。\n        我们对罗塞尔大帝的一生了解得还不够多，但我们知道他是——一个时代的开端，一个闪耀的传奇，一个永不褪色的名字。"] = "Roselle Gustav has been dead for over one hundred and fifty years, but his name has never been forgotten. \n In Trier, the capital of Intis, his statue still stands in the center of the square. Every year on his birthday, people hold grand events to commemorate him. In the factories of the Loen Kingdom, workers use the machines he invented, and children learn the knowledge he promoted in schools. Merchant ships in the Fog Sea sail along the routes he pioneered, and in the colonies of the Southern Continent, adventurers recount his legends. \n He was a transmigrator, a foreigner, a wanderer who could never return to his homeland. But he was also the Son of Steam, the Consul of the Intis Republic, Caesar the Great, Emperor Roselle, a powerful Beyonder, a father—a man who changed the entire world. \n He made mistakes, took detours, was corrupted, and was betrayed, eventually falling in the White Maple Palace. But he also created, protected, loved, and left behind the brilliance and civilization of an era. \n Perhaps as he wrote in his diary: if he could do it all over again, he might have chosen to be an ordinary person, returning to that world with fried chicken and cola, staying by his parents' side, and living an ordinary and warm life. But history has no 'ifs.' Roselle Gustav had no choice but to become the protagonist of the era. \n We do not know enough about Emperor Roselle's life, but we know what he was—the beginning of an era, a shining legend, a name that never fades.",
